{
 "file": "CDROM/FUKUTEST/MAINROM.NBN",
 "note": "main HUD sheet (boot_data_load -> 0x80180000; 13 4-bpp 128x128 pages of 8 KB, page n at n*0x2000, uploaded to 128x128 VRAM slots; CLUT rows = the 16 rows at D_800CC520 in the exe). Page 9 x96..121: the nine stat labels of the calendar / room panel (parameter_show_init draws them as class_w sprite frames, two 16-px tiles each; the labels sit in 26x12 cells 14 px apart). Page 4: digits 0-9 and 月 on rows 0-11, the weekday / unit kanji 火 水 木 金 土 日 年 on rows 16-27 (12x12 cells, 16-px pitch; hizuke_init: weekday = frame D_800EE7A1+82, the 年/月/日 units are fixed sprites). 日 is one cell serving both the day unit and Sunday, so it reads D in both places; 月 is Mo as the month unit and as Monday. Page 5 x 23..49, y 49..61: the red badge セーブ中 (saving) that replaces the night planner's save icon (bottom right of the icon grid, step 48) while the game writes the card; read on screen 2026-11-03 (explorer album:96/8/10 seed 2, frame 7050: the badge sits where the save icon was, right after the save icon is chosen) and on the page enlarged: セ, ー, ブ (the two dakuten dots), 中.  Drawn with exe CLUT row 13: ring 5, pink fills 7..10.  English SAVE. F2 (2026-11-06): Sunday no longer shares the day unit's cell. Tu and Sa are drawn as two 8-px tile halves (T|u, S|a; the second letter starts on the tile grid) so the exe's Sunday frame 88 (D_800CFC5C[88]) can be rebuilt as two cels, S (tile 0x28) + u (tile 0x21), a new record in the text module (pt_hud_sunday_frame, text_misc.c) with the frame pointer poked (config/patch/english.json main.pokes); the Tue / Sat frames' cel x moves left 2 / 1 px so the labels sit where the 12-px cells drew them.  The 日 cell keeps D as the day unit.",
